-- CAPABILITY --------- errors/cap_grant_exceeded_2.march

`main` is granted `needs IO.Console`, but the program reaches `IO.FileRead` (reached from `main`: main → slurp). The grant is a ceiling on the WHOLE program — declaring `needs IO.FileRead` does not raise it. [cap_grant_exceeded]
help: add `IO.FileRead` to `main`'s request (its `needs` clause, or the module's `needs` line when `main` has no clause), or request all of `IO`, or remove the use.

33 |   fn main() : () needs IO.Console do
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^


    fix (`forge fix` applies it):

33 -   fn main() : () needs IO.Console do
33 +   fn main() : () needs IO.Console, IO.FileRead do

    run `march --explain cap_grant_exceeded`


